{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy","id":1005413,"title":"A Mage's Guide to the Galaxy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-19T11:31:09-08:00","id":1005413,"title":"A Mage's Guide to the Galaxy","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Been reading over Book of Worlds and Infinite Tapestry and just wanted to try and get this all straight in my head.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">First of all, bellow is my understanding of the basic set up of Spiritual Cosmology</span></span><br /> <br /> Mundane Earth<br /> <br /> ==GAUNTLET==<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Penumbra</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-Astral Videre</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-Videre Spiritum (WtA penumbra)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-Videre Mortus (WtO shadowlands)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- The Dreaming (CtD &quot;penumbra&quot;)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Near Umbra</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-High Umbra</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-- Vulgate, Afterworlds, Spires, Courts, Epiphamies, etc.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Middle Umbra</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-- all the various realms such as Flux, Scar, the Aetherial Realm, the Abyss, etc.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-- many zones such as mirror zones, null zones, and vistas, the Digital Web, and the Maya (CtD).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Low/Dark Umbra</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-- the Tempest, the Isle of Sorrow, the Far Shores, the Yellow Springs, the Labyrinth, etc</span></span><br /> <br /> Grand connecting realms<br /> -- The Pattern Web, Alder Bole, Mount Qaf<br /> <br /> ==FIRST HORIZON== (Earths Atmosphere)<br /> <br /> Ether Space/True Horizon<br /> <br /> - Mundane Planets: Sun (maybe), Mercury, Venus, Luna, Mars<br /> <br /> - Shard Realms (planet penumbra),<br /> --Venus's realm of dinosaurs and varied biomes, where the Seasonal Realm used to be.<br /> --Luna's Spiritual realm, Arcadia (assumed), where the Dark Side VE base used to be.<br /> -- Mars's ancient civilisations, where Doissetep used to be.<br /> <br /> - Shade Realms<br /> -- S.R. Corr, (City of Brass turned Escher paradise)<br /> -- S.R. Life, (Evolution gone insane), where the seasonal realm used to be.<br /> -- S.R. Prime, (Possibly the entirety of the Umbra, especially the Aetherial Realm seen in WtA)<br /> -- S.R. Forces, (Energy gone mad), where Doissetep used to be.<br /> <br /> - Various Horizon Realms<br /> -- Seasonal Realm, Victoria Station, Balador, Gernsback, Autocthonia, etc.<br /> -- The Deep Dreaming (CtA)<br /> <br /> ==THE FAR HORIZON== (Asteroid Belt)<br /> <br /> Deep Umbra<br /> ((The distinction between mundane and spiritual planets breaks down here, if you believe you are in the umbra, you're in the umbra, if you believe you're in mundane space, you're in mundane space.))<br /> - Shard Realm<br /> -- Jupiter and it's (far too many) moons<br /> -- Saturn and it's (far fewer) moons<br /> -- Uranus<br /> -- Neptune<br /> -- Pluto<br /> -- The Shenti (Realms for the three Resonances)<br /> <br /> - Shade Realms<br /> -- S.R. Matter (Hollow Worlds (I like to imagine this as a &quot;space is solid rock, and solid rock is space&quot; inversion of our universe))<br /> -- S.R. Time (The Time Stream itself, best not to go here)<br /> -- S.R. Spirit (Seeking land with Avatar Influence)<br /> -- S.R. Mind (Seeking land with Internal Conflict)<br /> -- S.R. Entropy (A gateway/barrier/preview into any of the numerous &quot;end of the world&quot; scenarios we've found, Gehenna, Ragnarok, Oblivion, take your pick.) Probably where Vistas come from.<br /> <br /> - Alternate Realities<br /> -- Hyperion War Realm (Where all the Jupiter Moon space wars still continue)<br /> -- Philosophical Realms (Realms where non-canonical victories of Nephandi, Mage, Technocrat or Marauder over various Jupiter Moons has taken place)<br /> -- Paradox Realms<br /> -- The Deep Dreaming (CtA)<br /> <br /> - Deep Horizon Chantries<br /> -- The Corpernicus Institute<br /> -- Concordia<br /> -- Several Nephandi Labyrinth and Marauder refuges.<br /> <br /> Void<br /> - Everything Else<br /> <br /> ((I've decided to ignore Antihelios aka The Red Star since that was only introduced to foreshadow and bring about the various &quot;End of the World&quot; scenarios that were supposed to end the game line)).<br /> <br /> <br /> ++Methods of Travel++<br /> <br /> This is what I've gathered on how to get from the various A's to the numerous B's<br /> <br /> ==Barriers==<br /> <br /> --Gauntlet--<br /> <br /> Magic<br /> - Step Sideways (spirit 3) for Middle and High Umbra<br /> - Astral Project (Mind 4) for High Umbra<br /> - Astral Sojourn (Mind 4/Prime 2/Spirit 3) for Middle and High Umbra<br /> - Agama Sojourn (Entropy 4/ Life 2/Spirit 3) for Low Umbra<br /> <br /> Other<br /> - Gateways<br /> -- Shallowings<br /> - Dreaming for the Maya<br /> <br /> --First Horizon--<br /> <br /> Magic<br /> - Spirit 5 to open Anchorhead<br /> - Mind 5 to unteather<br /> <br /> Other<br /> - Use Spaceship to navigate Horizon<br /> - Search for cracks in the Horizon<br /> - Enter already opened Anchorheads.<br /> <br /> --Far Horizon--<br /> <br /> Pretty much the same as the above, but it's much more difficult and much more dangerous.<br /> <br /> Traversal thereafter can be via Ship, Projection, or simply &quot;walking&quot; across depending on how you view the universe.<br /> <br /> ==Corridors==<br /> <br /> These are alternative methods of traversal which get around some of the barriers above.<br /> <br /> - The Pattern Web - From any near umbra world to another<br /> - Alder Bole/Mount Qaf - Climb up to the high umbra, or down to the low umbra (find it's branches in the high and its roots in the low)<br /> - The Aetherial Realm - From the middle umbra to the very edge of the Deep Umbra. This allows direct entry into any of the Shade Realms provided the Spirits of each planet are happy with you, you can also access the Shenti from here. It should be possible to return to the &quot;normal&quot; deep umbra from here too, but then you're going to have a very hard time returning. Technomancers may never use this path.<br /> - The Maya - By entering the Near Dreaming, it is possible to navigate the various Trods and Pathways to get effectively anywhere in the Umbra, from the Near Umbra, to the Deep Dreaming. This is the most dangerous method of all as you have the least control over where you may end up, and can only be done by Dreamspeakers or by those with a Fae guide.<br /> <br /> ==Backdoors==<br /> <br /> Other little connecting methods that get around the more &quot;classical&quot; methods examined above. (some of these are just my own musings).<br /> <br /> - The Hollow Worlds - Perhaps by falling into the hollow world in Earth, provided you believe in the hollow earth theory and can be lucky enough to find a portal, you are then able to explore the Shade Realm of Matter, and with enough time can dig your way towards Jupiter, where you can exit in the Deep Umbra (this would probably take a great deal of time, and the chances of getting lost or stuck are much higher)<br /> - The Virtual Web - By fully entering the Virtual Web, you can then exit a module in Dystopia, one of the realms within the Middle Umbra.<br /> - The Afterworlds - There is a chance the Afterworlds of the High Umbra and the Far Shores of the Low Umbra take place in an overlapping realm, allowing a backdoor entry of sorts for Mages and Wraiths alike. Chances are such an overlap is not well advertised, and if it was it probably isn't all that easy to exploit.<br /> - Oblivion and S.R. Entropy - There is a chance that a link between these two distant areas exists, and that if one enters the S.R of Entropy, they may be able to emerge in the deepest depths of the True Malfean Labyrinth and the bottom of the Tempest, this may then indicate a reverse trip is possible, though the penalty for being wrong would be severe.<br /> <br /> Assuming that there are no convenient portals to such realms, these backdoor ideas give a wealth of possible traversal methods in order to get to specific yet almost unattainable locations.<br /> <br /> How viable do you guys think this may be? And what other methods are you aware of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T12:25:04-08:00","id":1005433,"title":"","content":"One good way to get PCs to another world is a suitable Talisman. Something an Archmage can make and certain mages or sleepers that can awake can use. Once you get your guys out there in the stars, either ignore discorperation or make the PCs immune to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T05:01:21-08:00","id":1005665,"title":"","content":"You actually forgot another backdoor that stretches across the Tellurian.<br /> <br /> The Null Zone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Singular.<br /> That weird maze of shafts and corridors where time does not seem to flow, magick does not work, technology breaks down, and each door can lead you anywhere else as you step out from 'Backstage' again. You just need to find the right one.<br /> Entering the Null Zone is done by focusing on getting 'Backstage' while sidestepping from the near umbra, and it's supposedly rather hard (High diff).<br /> <br /> But after that, you can go pretty much anywhere..if you can find it. There is debate wether the Null Zone is another aspect of Mount Qaf/The Alder Bole, a strange version of the old Paths of the Wyck, or something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T06:32:34-08:00","id":1005683,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> You're right, I completely forgot about that. I'd probably classify it as a &quot;corridor&quot; though as you could technically get anywhere from there. In many ways it's like the Maya/Dreaming, except way more imprecise and much easier to get trapped within.<br /> I've always imagined The Null Zone in the following way. Imagine a reality where the only things that actually exist if what you directly perceive. You look at the wall, and the moment you look away, the wall ceases to exist, but will return just as you look back. This happens with every sense, the moment you go out of earshot of something, that sound just stops, the moments you lift your foot of the ground, the floor beneath you ceases to be, and as long as you're not looking down, will not return until you place your foot back down.<br /> <br /> Reality is constantly shifting to meet what you expect to see. As a result the world is only &quot;part&quot; there. The far side of objects do not exist until you either feel them out of turn the object around. Similarly, if you go to look inside the boot of a car, anything you can't see, the front, the tires, the engine, ceases to exist until you return. The back of your head does no exist unless you feel it or someone else is looking at it.<br /> <br /> It's a perfect blend of the Metaphysical Trinity. Dynamics made by perception, Stasis enforced by expectation, and Entropy brought about as the perceiving body moves on.<br /> <br /> The Null Zone is then being able to see all of this from another perspective without influencing it at all. Depending on your paradigm you may see it all being held together by bits of string and wooden boards; portal like panels which spring up in response to how the &quot;perseveres&quot; move, like a video game from a noclip perspective; as a black void which only &quot;pops&quot; into place as people chat what they view; a mess of chaos which is forced into alignment in response to the will of the viewer; that there are Descartian demons and spirits throwing moving around packages of Sense Datum into appropriate locations at the correct times. It could be all of these methods are employed in various cases depending on what's required.<br /> <br /> Things can only &quot;be&quot; in this world if they are being seen, and this may mean that the vast majority of the world is dark with scant moments of activity depending on where any form of sentient minds linger. It could instead be a series of corridors that weave in all these minds, which in reality are right next to each other. Someone standing on the edge of Ganymede could be standing right next to someone in a library in Phoenix Arizona, but their senses don't allow such closeness to be usable.<br /> <br /> Again, depending on the paradigm, it might not just be Humans, of Sentient Creatures that are capable of perception, but that all living things have a hand in shaping the forms of the world, perhaps this rule even applies to spiritual entities, perhaps there is a greater being, a deity or group of deities who is able to perceive parts of or the entirety of the world at once, in such case the Null zone would be more like a &quot;hub&quot; point than a mass expanse of space or a winding section of corridors.<br /> Alternatively, it could be the only think that exists in reality is your own mind, and everything else is but a product of your own perceptions. This type of Null World would probably manifest similarly to the &quot;Deity&quot; one, except it is them that it in the centre of the hub and with no real knowledge on how to take control of anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 11-20-2016, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:50:00-08:00","id":1005815,"title":"","content":"What an unworkable internally inconsistent craptastic catastrophic mess of a cosmology! <br /> <br /> Thanks for putting that all together so I could finally see that my gut reaction to Mage's omniverse is correct and that it should be disassembled with an ax, the remains gone through with tweezers and the sane-ish bits that are picked out reassembled into something internally consistent and coherent. <br /> <br /> Oh and remotely functional in both crunch and fluff....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T13:05:25-08:00","id":1005824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1005815#post1005815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What an unworkable internally inconsistent craptastic catastrophic mess of a cosmology!<br /> <br /> Thanks for putting that all together so I could finally see that my gut reaction to Mage's omniverse is correct and that it should be disassembled with an ax, the remains gone through with tweezers and the sane-ish bits that are picked out reassembled into something internally consistent and coherent.<br /> <br /> Oh and remotely functional in both crunch and fluff....</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire game's like that. But then what do you expect with a system that's based around the idea &quot;What if everything anyone ever thought up was actually true! All of it!&quot;<br /> <br /> I think unworkable is a little strong though. I think all of it is pretty good for both lore and exciting places for the players to quest around.<br /> <br /> Personally, I really like the omniverse aspect of it all. There's so much stuff out there that literally anyone's interpretation of it can be considered canon, and what's more I think it does a good job of linking the various game lines together.<br /> <br /> Which pieces do you consider to be particularly unworkable by the way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 11-20-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T17:12:17-08:00","id":1005911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1005824#post1005824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The entire game's like that. But then what do you expect with a system that's based around the idea &quot;What if everything anyone ever thought up was actually true! All of it!&quot;<br /> <br /> I think unworkable is a little strong though. I think all of it is pretty good for both lore and exciting places for the players to quest around.<br /> <br /> Personally, I really like the omniverse aspect of it all. There's so much stuff out there that literally anyone's interpretation of it can be considered canon, and what's more I think it does a good job of linking the various game lines together.<br /> <br /> Which pieces do you consider to be particularly unworkable by the way?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it could be designed less like a party of rowdy toddlers were disemboweling an octopus filled with chocolate ice cream. I could expect an entire gaming company that came out with the tagline of &quot;Role-playing not ROLL-playing&quot; (the last with a condescending sneer) would not only avoid such a cesspool of incredibly baroque bad and overwrought rules for something that is intrinsic to the system. <br /> <br /> There is no problem having a wide-open universe. This is certainly not it. It's like looking a dozen ideas broken apart to one degree or another and connected by a web of Silly String. This mess isn't enabling. It's limiting in the extreme. Watch any discussion about how one aspect or another of the Umbra works. The Rules Police come out with their alarms blaring and shout down most original takes on what mages can do in &quot;places other than here&quot; and start throwing up walls around creativity by applying different rubrics, which are almost always mutually exclusive. Then the thread bogs down into which narrow crack of the Umbra rules this particular situation falls. <br /> <br /> And it's not even a complete cosmology as there are still wide open questions out there to which there is no good answer and some cases where the competing ideas get in the way of doing really cool things that seem completely mage-y. <br /> <br /> It's easier to pick out the ideas that are workable.<br /> <br /> The basic essential ideas of all those Indo-European threesomes seem like good basic structure: Penumbra-Umbra-Deep Umbra; High-Middle-Low. Then play &quot;pin the weird ass dimensional place&quot; on the continuum for most of the other others places. Things already get complicated at this point as the whole Conventional Space of the Union vs. the conceptualization of the other factions gets a little problematic, but not in an unsolvable (probably even easier to do now that the new definition given to the whole concept embedded into Focus might help that one out... or not, it might need to be something like a Z-axis to the to the X and Y of the above.). <br /> <br /> How about a single set of rules from traveling from HERE to THERE that weren't riddled with odd additions and rampant Sphere-bloat? (Which wouldn't be too hard if it's just Spirit 3 and the appropriate vidare to get to whatever Umbra fits with the mage in question. But.... nope. Here's a rule for this level of the Umbra. Here's a rule for that. And here's two sets of rules for this one thing that don't really make sense. And no rules for this. And some more rules for this oddity over here....)<br /> <br /> Honestly, I have only used what chunks of the Umbra made sense to the game I was playing, insofar as they make sense for that game. There's no way I would inflict that complete mess above. When the game was about Etherites in space, I didn't arbitarily divide the solar system into an Umbra half and a Deep Umbra half. They could take their spaceship and fly from Venus to the moons of Jupiter without needing Spirit 5 instead of Spirit 3. Because the game was about planet-hopping. Also, because it suited the way the universe worked best, &quot;Conventional Space&quot; off-planet was elastic enough that there could be space battles between Etherships with sails using Death Ray Hurlers and Void Engineers using fusion drives and electron-pumped X-ray lasers. Does that work with any of the Mage rules as written. Nope. Those two ships would be in separate layers of reality and would have to use Spirit to detect or affect each other. But it worked for the game. In fact it worked better than the rules would have, as it simplified some complexities that don't make sense except in a very weird look at the cosmos (which again, isn't an omniverse that frees one, it's a set of shackles to a very particular world view on which everything else needs to be tacked, whether or not it fits).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T18:33:11-08:00","id":1005929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1005911#post1005911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it could be designed less like a party of rowdy toddlers were disemboweling an octopus filled with chocolate ice cream. I could expect an entire gaming company that came out with the tagline of &quot;Role-playing not ROLL-playing&quot; (the last with a condescending sneer) would not only avoid such a cesspool of incredibly baroque bad and overwrought rules for something that is intrinsic to the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice bit of vitriol, this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1005911#post1005911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no problem having a wide-open universe. This is certainly not it. It's like looking a dozen ideas broken apart to one degree or another and connected by a web of Silly String. This mess isn't enabling. It's limiting in the extreme. Watch any discussion about how one aspect or another of the Umbra works. The Rules Police come out with their alarms blaring and shout down most original takes on what mages can do in &quot;places other than here&quot; and start throwing up walls around creativity by applying different rubrics, which are almost always mutually exclusive. Then the thread bogs down into which narrow crack of the Umbra rules this particular situation falls.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a framework, and the idea of it is to try and consolidate all of the existing WoD games into one continuous line of existence. Every game line has their own slice of Umbra, and Mages are the few who are able to (in theory) visit all of them.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not really all that possible to rule police the Umbra. The only general rules there are Matter, Forces, Life, and Time are a bit harder, Corr is just plain weird, Spirit becomes a swiss army knife of sorts, and prime is even shinier than usual. This is only not the case for the specifically mentioned Realms within the umbra, and on the whole they make intuitive sense. Of course Entropy is going to be super charged and a really bad idea in the Tempest, it makes sense that magic is not really possible it do in the Wasteland, and that it's harder at the foot of the Abyss, those are places of malice, hoplessness, and outright suffering. The magic reflects this.<br /> <br /> Bare in mind that the Middle Umbra is not just the various realms it contains, it's the spirit wilds and can be any kind of terrain you want it to be. Jungle, desert, meadow, tundra, whatever you want. If you wish to add weird restrictions on other magic effects, that's fine too. Otherwise, just stick with the basics, enjoy that most/all things are coincidental, and have fun with the eventual botched paradox backlash, this is your time to makes things <i>really</i> weird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1005911#post1005911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's not even a complete cosmology as there are still wide open questions out there to which there is no good answer and some cases where the competing ideas get in the way of doing really cool things that seem completely mage-y.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of questions do you have in mind?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1005911#post1005911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's easier to pick out the ideas that are workable.<br /> <br /> The basic essential ideas of all those Indo-European threesomes seem like good basic structure: Penumbra-Umbra-Deep Umbra; High-Middle-Low. Then play &quot;pin the weird ass dimensional place&quot; on the continuum for most of the other others places. Things already get complicated at this point as the whole Conventional Space of the Union vs. the conceptualization of the other factions gets a little problematic, but not in an unsolvable (probably even easier to do now that the new definition given to the whole concept embedded into Focus might help that one out... or not, it might need to be something like a Z-axis to the to the X and Y of the above.).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understand the problem here. It works more or less the same way anything in the consensus works. Conventional space is what modern education tells us to believe, and has become the default interpretation in the mind of the zeitgeist. The Umbral counterparts are the lost or diminished thoughts and beliefs of astrologers, seers, and astronomers alike. They become a step removed from reality as their prominence lessens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1005911#post1005911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a single set of rules from traveling from HERE to THERE that weren't riddled with odd additions and rampant Sphere-bloat? (Which wouldn't be too hard if it's just Spirit 3 and the appropriate vidare to get to whatever Umbra fits with the mage in question. But.... nope. Here's a rule for this level of the Umbra. Here's a rule for that. And here's two sets of rules for this one thing that don't really make sense. And no rules for this. And some more rules for this oddity over here....)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a really good reason for this. It shouldn't be easy or common for Mages to be spotted in other gamelines as often as all these sphere uses would imply. Similarly it should take quite a bit of dedication and hard work to be able to go to certain areas. For example, it makes sense you'd have to be half dead to enter the deadlands, just as Astral Projection makes sense as a method of reaching the high umbra. Astral Sojourn allows an alternative method to Stepping Sideways which comes with its own set of caveats. That's about it though, the only other methods are by entering what are essentially doors.<br /> <br /> Also, I think just having Spirit 3 be the universal key would somewhat demystify these realms. Having Agama Sojourn the only direct entryway into the deadlands makes them more unattainable, and thus more mysterious and tantalising. In order to get there, you need to either train specifically for the trip, find someone or something that can help you, or go out and quest for an alternative route. So many potential quest plots, all of which would be lost if it was just &quot;hey, I got spirit 3, we'll be there in a second!&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1005911#post1005911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I have only used what chunks of the Umbra made sense to the game I was playing, insofar as they make sense for that game. There's no way I would inflict that complete mess above. When the game was about Etherites in space, I didn't arbitarily divide the solar system into an Umbra half and a Deep Umbra half. They could take their spaceship and fly from Venus to the moons of Jupiter without needing Spirit 5 instead of Spirit 3. Because the game was about planet-hopping. Also, because it suited the way the universe worked best, &quot;Conventional Space&quot; off-planet was elastic enough that there could be space battles between Etherships with sails using Death Ray Hurlers and Void Engineers using fusion drives and electron-pumped X-ray lasers. Does that work with any of the Mage rules as written. Nope. Those two ships would be in separate layers of reality and would have to use Spirit to detect or affect each other. But it worked for the game. In fact it worked better than the rules would have, as it simplified some complexities that don't make sense except in a very weird look at the cosmos (which again, isn't an omniverse that frees one, it's a set of shackles to a very particular world view on which everything else needs to be tacked, whether or not it fits).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine. You can do whatever you want to service your game. Though by removing restrictions you also lose a level of potential conflict.<br /> <br /> The divide of the Deep Umbra isn't arbitrary, it's along the Astroid Belt, a pretty natural place for a barrier to be put if anywhere. The big difference between the True Horizon and the Deep Umbra is simply that in the deep umbra, there is not real distinction between mundane and umbral, everything is all a mesh unto itself. The moment you cross the far horizon, you're in the realm of anything goes so long as you can imagine and believe it.<br /> <br /> If you wanted, you could just have your Etherites have a Spirit 5 Break the Dream Shell style talisman attached to it. You'd have needed such a thing to get past the Near Horizon barrier anyway, so it's sort of a moot point. Again, getting rid of the Far Horizon barrier makes the Deep Umbra much less mysterious and reviled. It goes from being &quot;Woah, things are getting serious&quot; to &quot;Ok everyone! We're off to Jupiter!!&quot;. If that's the tone you're going for then fine, but I prefer my space exploration to be filled with uncertainty and constant moments of &quot;is this really a good idea?&quot;. These obstacles provide a necessity for the players to think about their options, to consider how they might approach rather than just swoop in guns blazing.<br /> Perhaps they could look for a powerful mage who can assist with these barriers, perhaps they could ask a spirit to help, maybe there's a way through if you just navigate well enough, maybe a quick pit stop in Mars could drum up some hints, maybe we could get their via the Hollow Worlds and dig our way to triumph!<br /> <br /> And yeah, because the Deep Umbra has no real distinction of conventional and umbral, those two ships would be in exactly the same place for their fights. It's only things like the Hyperion realm, the Shade Realms, the Philosophical Realms, and the various lost Horizon realms which would require flying into bubbles of reality. Otherwise you're in deep space.<br /> This could be another thing which adds layers of &quot;what's going on?&quot; to the players. A void engineer ship approaches, but are they from the same Earth as they? Are they a historic vessel from the Hyperion Realm? Do they perhaps hail from an alternate future via the Shade Realm of Time? Did we accidentally fly into a Philosophical Realm where the Technocracy won and have started to colonise space? or perhaps one where the Void Engineers and the Etherites are still allies? Lots of things to consider, lots of possibility for peril.<br /> <br /> Barriers like these are meant to be restrictions for the player, but tools for the ST to add extra intrigue and puzzle to the adventure. It's a case of &quot;Everything is possible to reach, but if you want to get there, you'd better work for it!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:04:02-08:00","id":1035824,"title":"","content":"Given that in M:tA Metaphorical can mean actual playing with old metaphors recycled in SciFi would be a quick way out into the Galaxy. The role given <b>Islands</b> in so many types of fiction is given to planets in SciFi. Heck Forbidden Planet is simply a reworking of the Tempest. The Mage20 book explicitly says that the Deep Sea and Deep Space are linked. Let that Island vacation land the PCs in the middle of a Space Opera!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:57:49-08:00","id":1037563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1005929#post1005929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That's fine. You can do whatever you want to service your game. Though by removing restrictions you also lose a level of potential conflict.<br /> <br /> The divide of the Deep Umbra isn't arbitrary, it's along the Astroid Belt, a pretty natural place for a barrier to be put if anywhere. The big difference between the True Horizon and the Deep Umbra is simply that in the deep umbra, there is not real distinction between mundane and umbral, everything is all a mesh unto itself. The moment you cross the far horizon, you're in the realm of anything goes so long as you can imagine and believe it.<br /> <br /> If you wanted, you could just have your Etherites have a Spirit 5 Break the Dream Shell style talisman attached to it. You'd have needed such a thing to get past the Near Horizon barrier anyway, so it's sort of a moot point. Again, getting rid of the Far Horizon barrier makes the Deep Umbra much less mysterious and reviled. It goes from being &quot;Woah, things are getting serious&quot; to &quot;Ok everyone! We're off to Jupiter!!&quot;. If that's the tone you're going for then fine, but I prefer my space exploration to be filled with uncertainty and constant moments of &quot;is this really a good idea?&quot;. These obstacles provide a necessity for the players to think about their options, to consider how they might approach rather than just swoop in guns blazing.<br /> Perhaps they could look for a powerful mage who can assist with these barriers, perhaps they could ask a spirit to help, maybe there's a way through if you just navigate well enough, maybe a quick pit stop in Mars could drum up some hints, maybe we could get their via the Hollow Worlds and dig our way to triumph!<br /> <br /> And yeah, because the Deep Umbra has no real distinction of conventional and umbral, those two ships would be in exactly the same place for their fights. It's only things like the Hyperion realm, the Shade Realms, the Philosophical Realms, and the various lost Horizon realms which would require flying into bubbles of reality. Otherwise you're in deep space.<br /> This could be another thing which adds layers of &quot;what's going on?&quot; to the players. A void engineer ship approaches, but are they from the same Earth as they? Are they a historic vessel from the Hyperion Realm? Do they perhaps hail from an alternate future via the Shade Realm of Time? Did we accidentally fly into a Philosophical Realm where the Technocracy won and have started to colonise space? or perhaps one where the Void Engineers and the Etherites are still allies? Lots of things to consider, lots of possibility for peril.<br /> <br /> Barriers like these are meant to be restrictions for the player, but tools for the ST to add extra intrigue and puzzle to the adventure. It's a case of &quot;Everything is possible to reach, but if you want to get there, you'd better work for it!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be completely frank, you don't know what you're talking about when you start talking about how I ran my game, selected which rules did and did not apply and did so in such a way as to make the stories we, as a team. were creating. No &quot;opportunities for conflict&quot; lost. Some that make no sense are avoided. There are tons of problems with the system as is that gets in the way of many, many, many (most) types of Outer Space, Space Opera to competence porn. This game you are borderline disparaging is regarded by those who remember it VERY fondly as one of the most &quot;Mage&quot; of all the Mage games we've played over a couple of decades, and, to several, is the best Mage game we ever played.<br /> <br /> There is no reason the Asteroid Belt makes any sort of sense as a boundary except that someone set it that way in 1st Ed. It's about as arbitrary as anything can be and fits with a particular view of the setting of mage that is more than a little wonky. Having most of the Solar System in the Deep Umbra makes the Deep Umbra the kind of loose and difficult to encompass concept that makes this an endless source of fruitless discussion. Why does Jupiter need to be in the Deep Umbra? Is there something completely different about Jovian space? Do the moons occasionally eat each other or change into conceptual matrices? Do planet-sized Cthuloid monsters swim in the Red Spot? Do mortal astronomers just not notice this in ANY way even though the whole point of letting the pesky mundanes have those telescopes is to reinforce the Tychoidean paradigm? If there's a &quot;natural&quot; place to put the boundary between Conventional Space and the Deep Umbra with regard to Conventional Space it's at the heliopause. That makes a TON more sense than the Asteroid Belt. In fact, those VE's have been pushing that all that stuff past the heliopause is deep or interstellar space. And the boundary between other Umbrae and the Deep Umbra occur along their own &quot;natural&quot; fission lines. And, probably, all those Deep Umbrae are the same Deep Umbra. <br /> <br /> Saying, that not using all of these rules so that you can make the lives of the players more complicated, or, apparently, not letting it be too easy for my lazy-minded players just rings false. The Umbra travel rules are completely arbitrary, ridiculously baroque and completely self-contradictory. If you actually start running a game that involves a lot of Umbral travel using all those rules, you will have to make concessions. 100% will HAVE to. There are just places they don't play well together. There are also tons of neat little gaps between the finicky little specific rules sets that your game will fall into sooner than you think and you'll be backpeddling and wasting valuable playing time or having to riff it all out. In addition, you will be spending LOTS of time having to manage a corpus of rules scattered across several different sources in a gaming milieu that began with the &quot;simplify all the fiddly rules so we can get to role-playing, not roll-playing&quot;. <br /> <br /> It all smacks of defending the status quo simply because it is the status quo and refusing to examine it for possible flaws and seeing if the game might be improved by doing so. And rigidly applying that status quo to a set of games predicated on the Golden Rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:49:09-08:00","id":1037598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1037563#post1037563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, to be completely frank, you don't know what you're talking about when you start talking about how I ran my game, selected which rules did and did not apply and did so in such a way as to make the stories we, as a team. were creating. No &quot;opportunities for conflict&quot; lost. Some that make no sense are avoided. There are tons of problems with the system as is that gets in the way of many, many, many (most) types of Outer Space, Space Opera to competence porn. This game you are borderline disparaging is regarded by those who remember it VERY fondly as one of the most &quot;Mage&quot; of all the Mage games we've played over a couple of decades, and, to several, is the best Mage game we ever played.<br /> <br /> There is no reason the Asteroid Belt makes any sort of sense as a boundary except that someone set it that way in 1st Ed. It's about as arbitrary as anything can be and fits with a particular view of the setting of mage that is more than a little wonky. Having most of the Solar System in the Deep Umbra makes the Deep Umbra the kind of loose and difficult to encompass concept that makes this an endless source of fruitless discussion. Why does Jupiter need to be in the Deep Umbra? Is there something completely different about Jovian space? Do the moons occasionally eat each other or change into conceptual matrices? Do planet-sized Cthuloid monsters swim in the Red Spot? Do mortal astronomers just not notice this in ANY way even though the whole point of letting the pesky mundanes have those telescopes is to reinforce the Tychoidean paradigm? If there's a &quot;natural&quot; place to put the boundary between Conventional Space and the Deep Umbra with regard to Conventional Space it's at the heliopause. That makes a TON more sense than the Asteroid Belt. In fact, those VE's have been pushing that all that stuff past the heliopause is deep or interstellar space. And the boundary between other Umbrae and the Deep Umbra occur along their own &quot;natural&quot; fission lines. And, probably, all those Deep Umbrae are the same Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> Saying, that not using all of these rules so that you can make the lives of the players more complicated, or, apparently, not letting it be too easy for my lazy-minded players just rings false. The Umbra travel rules are completely arbitrary, ridiculously baroque and completely self-contradictory. If you actually start running a game that involves a lot of Umbral travel using all those rules, you will have to make concessions. 100% will HAVE to. There are just places they don't play well together. There are also tons of neat little gaps between the finicky little specific rules sets that your game will fall into sooner than you think and you'll be backpeddling and wasting valuable playing time or having to riff it all out. In addition, you will be spending LOTS of time having to manage a corpus of rules scattered across several different sources in a gaming milieu that began with the &quot;simplify all the fiddly rules so we can get to role-playing, not roll-playing&quot;.<br /> <br /> It all smacks of defending the status quo simply because it is the status quo and refusing to examine it for possible flaws and seeing if the game might be improved by doing so. And rigidly applying that status quo to a set of games predicated on the Golden Rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:46:05-08:00","id":1037636,"title":"","content":"Well, you can look at WtA, where you have Outer Space, the Aetherial Realm, and the Deep Umbra. Jupiter exists in all three (the physical body in Outer Space, the Jupiter Realm in the Aetherial Realm, and the Jupiter Realm in the Deep Umbra). In the perspective of WtA, the Mages prevent themselves from accessing the Deep Umbra before the Asteroid Belt or Outer Space beyond the Asteroid Belt, as the beliefs of the Mages prevent them from interacting with Outer Space or the Deep Umbra except for where they believe they can interact with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T09:22:19-08:00","id":1037871,"title":"","content":"The problem with the Mage cosmology is actually quite a large one. It's premise is fundamentally that the Solar System as seen by scientists on Earth is the TRUTH. There IS an Asteroid Belt. There IS a division between the inner and outer Solar System. Mars, Venus and Mercury ARE rocky small planets, Saturn, Jupiter, Neptune and Uranus ARE gas giants and Pluto IS something else. And so on. All the mage-specific folderol is tacked onto that. The Asteroid Belt is the Horizon. Horizon Realms are actually located on Asteroids and on or around inner system planets. And so on. <br /> <br /> That's a HUGE problem because it essentially picks one view of the universe and deems it CORRECT. And that POV is the Technocratic one. That means they're right and everyone else is wrong. The best you can do is try to play &quot;pin my cosmology on the planets&quot;. (It also causes a few more crossover problems than already exist because it's pretty difficult to square, say the Werewolf cosmology with Mage's at all, as Aya points out.... And Mage is supposed to be expansive in it's ability to accommodate various belief systems.) <br /> <br /> For example: Doissetep is on Mars. It might be a slightly off-kilter Mars, one step over from the one with the Rover on it. Or not. But that doesn't matter really, because it is definitely not the Mars of the Ptolemaic model of the Solar System with all the chiming ethereal crystal spheres in an interlocking divine celestial Antikytheria Device writ cosmic. So the &quot;Mars&quot; of the Tychoidean system is the REAL Mars and the best the Traditions can do is go to their Mars and wriggle a little to find an amenable dimensional pocket. What has that Mars got to do with the ethos/uber-paradigm/praxis of the Hermetics? And it starts getting much much worse when you start taking into account beleif structures that would be better served by something more akin to the Werewolf model for various cultures, mythologies, belief systems and magical practices around the world. Like, say, many, many, many of different groups that were jammed together as the Dreamspeakers. Mars may not even BE a place. It may be a person who wanders across the fields that we percieve as the night sky. A Dreamspeaker might not magically conceive of a trip to a place called &quot;Mars&quot; (appropriately translated), they would being going to talk to someone who is that red dot in the sky.... And they would never be &quot;walking through outer space&quot; to get there (making for something fairly odd to throw up on the screen of Voidship command deck....) They would step sideways and find/take the way to where one can wander the &quot;Fields of Night&quot; or what have you. <br /> <br /> The only reason to hold onto this seems to be inertia. That's the way they first thought of it as a stab at a compromise of belief systems. But Mage has moved WAY past the way they were originally thinking in any number of ways. Look back at what &quot;paradigm&quot; meant and didn't mean in first edition compared to 2nd, Revised or M20. There's been evolution of the way the ideas have been handled and paradigm/ethos/Focus have moved from being decorative to a central focus. There should be a similar evolution here. And it would MASSIVELY simplify this boondoggle.<br /> <br /> What is Conventional Space? It's the slice of the Umbra that the Technocrats are exploring. It's THEIR Umbra. Other groups have different but equally valid ways of perceiving and interacting with the heavens that are appropriate to them. Why do all us (Western, scientifically literate) mortals think of Conventional Space as the Truth? Because that's what the Union and the Order have been selling us all the way back to when the Celestial Masters, who were not just looking at THE Truth, but seeking for A truth that worked for them, and those magical optical devices along with all the related paraphernalia is what the Consensus bought lock, stock, barrel and Toys R Us kid's first telescope. But that doesn't mean that an Etherite is going to go up into &quot;Space&quot; and not find something more like Barsoom than what the Mars Rover is sending back pictures of, nor that a Hermetic might end up &quot;going into space&quot; in way that seems more like a Baron Munchausen story or something similar to Dante, with various realms that have to be appropriately traversed to go from level to level of the Ptolemaic system....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T10:28:45-08:00","id":1037900,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1062_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1062\" data-vbnamecard=\"1062\">Ajax</a> It kind of seems to me as though you're making this into a bigger problem than it needs to be.<br /> <br /> Conventional space is the Technocratic model of the universe, but who's to say that in the umbra, the old models that the traditions cling to isn't still the case?<br /> Perhaps an Etherite can traverse the Geocentric solar system, and a Dreamspeaker may walk to the people as planets. Nothing in the books says this cannot be the case.<br /> <br /> In mage, especially in the umbra, it's generally a case of expectation guiding what you experience. What's the problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T10:44:11-08:00","id":1037910,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's say we could just chuck out what's already there and reformulate it to be whatever we thought best fit Mage. What would this new Umbra look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:16:44-08:00","id":1038064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1037900#post1037900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1062_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1062\" data-vbnamecard=\"1062\">Ajax</a> It kind of seems to me as though you're making this into a bigger problem than it needs to be.<br /> <br /> Conventional space is the Technocratic model of the universe, but who's to say that in the umbra, the old models that the traditions cling to isn't still the case?<br /> Perhaps an Etherite can traverse the Geocentric solar system, and a Dreamspeaker may walk to the people as planets. Nothing in the books says this cannot be the case.<br /> <br /> In mage, especially in the umbra, it's generally a case of expectation guiding what you experience. What's the problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>And now you seem to be taking the same position I have been holding forth. Don't take the situation as presented for granted. As is, the system is the accretion of ALL the bits that ever were and an attempt to bind them together with spit and baling wire. But this is a departure from that. Up until that post, you haven't seemed willing to budge from the setting/rules as written and look at the whole situation any other way. Because once you have shaman going on visionquests to talk to Mars, a Mars that is just a valid and real and manifest as the Red Planet in our telescopes, you're coloring outside the lines. That's NOT the way the situation is set up. That's NOT RAW. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:18:39-08:00","id":1038065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1037910#post1037910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, let's say we could just chuck out what's already there and reformulate it to be whatever we thought best fit Mage. What would this new Umbra look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on what you want to accomplish? The thread is titled &quot;A Guide to Galaxy&quot;? Is that the perspective we're working from? Because that starts you from a different place than &quot;In the Beginning, there were 3 Umbrae: The High, the Middle and the Low....&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:20:12-08:00","id":1038066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1038065#post1038065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That depends on what you want to accomplish? The thread is titled &quot;A Guide to Galaxy&quot;? Is that the perspective we're working from? Because that starts you from a different place than &quot;In the Beginning, there were 3 Umbrae: The High, the Middle and the Low....&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It was just a pop culture reference... geez.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:33:08-08:00","id":1038075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1038066#post1038066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was just a pop culture reference... geez.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's 100% relevant. If you want to start from the technomantic side of things, it's a good a place as any, but you might end up at a different destination than if you start with the Trifold Umbra and start working out from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:42:37-08:00","id":1038082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1038065#post1038065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That depends on what you want to accomplish? The thread is titled &amp;quot;A Guide to Galaxy&amp;quot;? Is that the perspective we're working from? Because that starts you from a different place than &amp;quot;In the Beginning, there were 3 Umbrae: The High, the Middle and the Low....&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's say that everywhere a typical sleeper cannot go is on the table, and the goal is to handle as many classic, cultural, metaphysical and other locales in as cohesive a manner as possible. <br /> <br /> Probably also a good idea to define how gonzo we want things to be. I love a good interstellar battle mansion, but that's not to everyone's taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T08:31:13-08:00","id":1038919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1038082#post1038082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's say that everywhere a typical sleeper cannot go is on the table, and the goal is to handle as many classic, cultural, metaphysical and other locales in as cohesive a manner as possible.<br /> <br /> Probably also a good idea to define how gonzo we want things to be. I love a good interstellar battle mansion, but that's not to everyone's taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, at stab at a first definition then:<br /> <br /> &quot;Everywhere a typical sleeper cannot go&quot; <br /> <br /> What does that mean? I would argue that, in the case of Conventional/Tychoidean/Technocratic Space (e.g. the Umbral Realm that accommodates that model.... which would be the &quot;classic solar system&quot; out to Pluto.... I would draw the line with the Deep Umbra for that conceptualization in such a way as the weirdness of the Oort Cloud, etc. is the weirdness of the Deep Umbra, while the very well examined Outer Solar System, back to Celestial Masters like Copernicus and Galileo, is still &quot;inside&quot; that boundary), a &quot;typical Sleeper&quot; doesn't really get above the higher cruising altitudes of aircraft. Which means all the satellites, LEO, the ISS, the Moon,etc. even the higher levels of the atmosphere proper (including the Heavyside Layewr) are all &quot;in the Umbra&quot; (or Penumbral/transitional, probably) and the folks who have gone there have been Enlightened Scientists, Extraordinary Citizens or well-prepared (and Conditioned) Sympathizers.<br /> <br /> For the other Umbral realms, there really haven't been anything more than sporadic occasions where typical mortals have strayed into them through unusual circumstances. (E.g. getting whisked off to the Crystal Spheres as per Kepler's little bit of sci-fi, the Baron Muchausen stories, even Dante's three part Odyssey, a lot of alien abductions, etc.) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:39:37-08:00","id":1039501,"title":"","content":"So separate the realms which can be perceived and studied from the earth? A Celestial Umbra, which contains the ways the physical universe could work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T11:25:39-08:00","id":1039525,"title":"","content":"The problem about Mage <i><u>Consensus</u></i>, so, what <i>most</i> people think that is... It is.<br /> <br /> So, in the beggining, the stars were just &quot;holes in the firmament&quot;. Even the planets weren't there. And the Earth REALLY WERE THE CENTER OF THE UNIVERSE.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Earth was flat, back in the day.<br /> <br /> But, the OoR came, and *PLIM!!! That tiny little red dot became a <u>material</u> world almost as big as Earth, courtesy of Galilleo.<br /> <br /> And the Explorers of the Void made Earth round, by convincing people of it (or maybe it isn't really round, it's just that when you go to one of the edges, you return in another. Space is an illusion, after all).<br /> <br /> After that, came the laws of Physics, telescopes, NASA... And those dots on the sky turned into MATERIAL celestial corpses.<br /> <br /> It's either that, or... Or they were always material to begin with. They were never holes in the sky, no matter how the first people believed in that.<br /> <br /> Or maybe, the Deep Umbra is not subjective to OUR perceptions. It's all well and good inside our neighborhood, but out there, it's ANOTHER Consensus. Of course, when we &quot;infect&quot; the outer space with our perceptions, we change the local Consensus as we go... But the rest of the Universe works without needing our eyes.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Universe works with the Consensus of many alien races? Their believes sending &quot;reality waves&quot; all over the universe, like cosmic radiation?<br /> <br /> Maybe that's also one of the reason that some Deep Umbra aliens try to invade Earth... Perhaps our race is disturbing the Galactic Consensus with our crazy ideas... And the Galactic Technocracy of the &quot;Greys&quot; want to end that &quot;reality anomaly&quot; Lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:02:30-08:00","id":1040068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1039525#post1039525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem about Mage <i><u>Consensus</u></i>, so, what <i>most</i> people think that is... It is.<br /> <br /> So, in the beggining, the stars were just &quot;holes in the firmament&quot;. Even the planets weren't there. And the Earth REALLY WERE THE CENTER OF THE UNIVERSE.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Earth was flat, back in the day.<br /> <br /> But, the OoR came, and *PLIM!!! That tiny little red dot became a <u>material</u> world almost as big as Earth, courtesy of Galilleo.<br /> <br /> And the Explorers of the Void made Earth round, by convincing people of it (or maybe it isn't really round, it's just that when you go to one of the edges, you return in another. Space is an illusion, after all).<br /> <br /> After that, came the laws of Physics, telescopes, NASA... And those dots on the sky turned into MATERIAL celestial corpses.<br /> <br /> It's either that, or... Or they were always material to begin with. They were never holes in the sky, no matter how the first people believed in that.<br /> <br /> Or maybe, the Deep Umbra is not subjective to OUR perceptions. It's all well and good inside our neighborhood, but out there, it's ANOTHER Consensus. Of course, when we &quot;infect&quot; the outer space with our perceptions, we change the local Consensus as we go... But the rest of the Universe works without needing our eyes.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Universe works with the Consensus of many alien races? Their believes sending &quot;reality waves&quot; all over the universe, like cosmic radiation?<br /> <br /> Maybe that's also one of the reason that some Deep Umbra aliens try to invade Earth... Perhaps our race is disturbing the Galactic Consensus with our crazy ideas... And the Galactic Technocracy of the &quot;Greys&quot; want to end that &quot;reality anomaly&quot; Lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. Maybe not. There are things the Consensus doesn't affect. There are baseline reality things. Like &quot;Earth&quot;. Another of those baselines things is &quot;Umbra&quot;. People can't just &quot;believe it away&quot;. Gods know the Technocracy has tried. Or maybe not, since they LIE, LIE, LIE about things they can't manage to control (like the possibility of people other than themselves being able to alter reality the way they can). The Technocracy at the higher levels almost certainly knows they can't get the Consensus to Unbelieve the Umbra out of existence. They can make them much harder to access by spreading those ideas, but they are still out there. Or make them easier to access by pushing a particular viewpoint. <br /> <br /> Whatever a Consensus might believe (since there wasn't one until very recently, and even then, not so much as the game tries to kludge it, not with &quot;Reality Zones&quot; and huge swaths of everything where it doesn't apply, like all those Umbras) would then define which Umbra it was easier for them to access. Of course the Earth was the Center of everything to almost all groups for almost all time. It WAS to them. Since that's how they accessed everything else. (And. TBH, Earth really still is the center of Reality even in the Tychoidean Model, even if it may orbit something else, it's pretty much singular in it's importance. The Union's model just pushes a certain way of believing one can interact with that particular flavor of the Umbra). The Earth was flat to those people because that was the way in which they interacted with all that was not-Earth, or, because there was absolutely no importance to their belief in the shape of Earth because it didn't affect them in any way at all. Meaning, if you asked any random person, they would probably scratch their heads because they had never thought about it and didn't really have a belief about it. And asking the question and giving them your answer didn't really affect the version of the Consensus to which that person belonged unless you could convince most, if not all, of those people.<br /> <br /> So, yup, there were holes in the sky to those people for whom holes in the sky were the way they dealt with &quot;that which is the Universe that is not-Earth&quot;. And there were planets of some sort out there in some way (since ideas can exist irrespective of whether they are actually currently held.... the OoR &quot;discovered&quot; the Tychoidean Model, but it was already out there in a transtemporal fashion, just no one knew about it until someone &quot;thought it up&quot; [that's the fun of the High Umbra, you might find places/ideas that haven't been thought up yet, just like you can find ideas that have been forgotten, but when you find them, you sorta thought them up... except for the fact that they are there, not always just in the initial Eureka format, but in a holistic fashion that can be explored.... e.g. your idea will have nooks and crannies (and planets) to explore that you never actually imagined that you imagined)... Just like the Celestial Master's model later has split off different versions which embrace what kids can see through their holiday gift telescopes and where NASA is sending probes, but there are SoE versions where there are canals on Mars and dinosaurs on Venus) which are not the same as the ones the Garou et al. go to which are not the same (though sometimes there is some overlap) with those that different subsets of Dreamspeakers and/or other similar mystic groups who are not joiners, access which are different than the chiming crystal spheres of the Ptolemaic Model(s), some of which are tagged in a fashion that is Kabbalah-friendly, some of which are all alchemical,, which are different than the models accessed by various faiths (like a Dante version of the universe), etc.<br /> <br /> As to what the Deep Umbra is.... Well, I buy the part about it being &quot;what is beyond the Consensus&quot;, as much in the fact that is may not be just the &quot;unknown&quot; but the &quot;unknowable&quot;. That's why it lends itself so easily to Lovecraftian things. The idea of a Sci-fi Galactic Consensus out there, sounds like an interesting idea, but it seems more like a seed for a specific idea for a specific version of the WoD for a specific sort of story and not what we've seen in the various mass of messy source material out there. In essence, currently, it's a good a card toss in the hat as a lot of other ideas, not as good as some (for which there is evidence) and better than others...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:33:58-08:00","id":1040623,"title":"","content":"It's always rubbed me the wrong way that the High Umbra contained all the conceptual models of the Solar System that weren't in vogue. I can't argue with the logic, the models are ideas after all, but the demarcation seems a bit abrupt. I have much the same feeling about all the old gods being High Umbrood. I think that's why I suggested a Celestial Umbra that contained most of the variants. It gives them more of a presence and possibly more meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T12:40:37-07:00","id":1300909,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that the planets are physical manifestations of god corpses because people stopped believing in them as gods and the result is that by knowing their True Name, the idea of the god was co-opted/corrupted into a material floating corpse in the Umbra (Space).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, there was a lot of confusion in this thread about how the Umbra is so inconsistent and doesn't make sense with how WILDLY varied it is, especially including crossovers of the other games. Well... I don't think it's hard to put it into a model that fits.<br /> <br /> Ready?<br /> <br /> Rule 1 of the Umbra - Be prepared to be surprised because the Umbra CHANGES according to who is visiting it and what you expect. It's very nature reflects reality. No two people see one thing exactly the same in the real world. Why would the Umbra, which changes according to expectation and other factors, even BE mappable or quantifiable where naming, direction, and manifestation are possible?<br /> <br /> Obviously it's not. Sure, it's a cheap idea but someone else said it best.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy?p=1005824#post1005824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The entire game's like that. But then what do you expect with a system that's based around the idea &quot;What if everything anyone ever thought up was actually true! All of it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Having it make sense is a job for the Order of Hermes and the Technocracy. Naming it pollutes it. Naming it gives it order. Naming it quantifies it. Naming it... gives it a name. If I were to profess an ideaology within mage, I would say don't name it. Don't create statis in the universe. Let the wonder remain! That IS the wonder of Mage. The wonder of magic. And that is precisely why it is magical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13189,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","user":"Knowledgeseeker","date":". 03-29-2019, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T11:00:20-07:00","id":1301350,"title":"","content":"For my own games, I tend to adapt a system like the following, which may or may not be tweaked, fiddled with, spun, folded, and/or mutilated depending on the needs of the specific chronicle. <br /> <br /> There is the Material World, obviously, and then the Gauntlet, which can be crossed using Spirit 3 rotes, certain Talismans, and the occasional established Gateway. There are also Shallowings, where the Gauntlet is freakishly thin, often to the point where mundane people can accidentally cross over. (These tend to be in very out of the way places like the middle of deserts, isolated mountain passes, hidden forest paths, out in the ocean, or even outer space, as well as mysterious back alleys, forgotten catacomb tunnels or the like.) There is also the use of Astral Projection to reach certain places. <br /> <br /> On the Other Side of the Gauntlet is the psycho-spiritual reflection of the Material World. Emotions, history, and spiritual forces color, alter and warp what is here, and for the Awakened, it is a blend of what the werewolves, ghosts and changelings experience (primal elementals, weird conceptual beings, echoes of the past, etc.). Mages who study other supernaturals or who work to refine their understanding of the Other Side sometimes refer to the Penumbra (the reflection of Life which the were beasts are tied to), the Shadowlands (the reflection of Death inhabited by the restless dead) and the Astral Mirror (the reflection of Mind that is the Near Dreaming of the fey). And yes, Mages can be strongly attuned to one of the three depending on personality, paradigm, Essence, Tradition and other factors. <br /> <br /> When you leave the immediate reflection of the Other Side, you enter the Other Worlds and their established Realms. The Skyvault, for example, is a long established place of astrological wisdom and celestial navigation, and also serves as a gateway to the Planetary Realms of the solar system. Each planet has a number of Realms connected to it. Each has the realm associated with one of the nine Spheres: Sun/Prime, Mercury/Connection, Venus/Life, Earth/Spirit, Moon/Mind, Mars/Forces, The Astroid Belt/Fate, Jupiter/Matter, Saturn/Time. Most also have a &quot;Court of the Gods&quot;, such as the Sun Gods, Pleasure, Witches, Earth Mothers, Battle, Kings, Endings, etc.. Venus, Earth, the Moon, and Mars also have Bygone versions, reflecting older visions of what those places were like, usually in older scientific romances and pulp adventure stories, though the Bygone Earth is a pre-human place of primordial forests, great beasts and super predators. And each has its unique realms, such as the Sun's Heavenly Gates, Mercury's lost Oasis of the Stars, Earth's Seasonal Realms and the Hollow Earth, Coyote's lunar Crashpad, and Jupiter's many moons, among others. <br /> <br /> Then there's the Astral Planes, full of nearly everything imaginable. The enigmatic faerie realms known as the Arcadian Gateways, the Endless Archive of all knowledge sitting on the banks of the River of Language, The Babylon Metropolis representing the very idea of cities, the Inventorium, the battlegrounds of Armageddon/The Planes of War, the Lands of Nod, the Hall of Mirrors, the Mythlands, and the various Zietheims such as the Gernsback Continuum, Ye Olde England, Dixie, and Suburbia. <br /> <br /> And the Heavens and Hells, the slightly enigmatic Realms which reflect human beliefs of paradise and punishment, which seem to straddle the Astral Realms and the Deathlands of Wraith (and sometimes even that of Werewolf's Umbra). These include the fire and brimstone of Infernia, the cold subterranean prisons of Tartarus, the baroque torture chambers of the Palace of Pleasure, and the predatory terror of the Hunting Grounds, as well as the perfect cosmic order of Utopia, the perfect light and bliss of the Radiance, the naturalistic paradise fo the Elysium Fields, and the comfort of The Last Tavern where everyone knows your name. <br /> <br /> Then there's the Deepest Depths, the far edges of reality, often beyond human understanding. These are realms of pure Chaos, Stasis and Corruption, cancers within the Tapestry itself (such as the Great Chasm and the Endless Labyrinth), and even the secret &quot;behind the curtain&quot; framework of the Tapestry. <br /> <br /> And past that is The Great Beyond, outside of our reality and dwelling place of alien horror and the secret masters of the Nephandi. <br /> <br /> That's my usual set up, at least. I don't think there's really any wrong way to do it as long as everyone at the table is having fun. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}